course: dictionary
lesson: 8320
title: Robust: strong, sturdy and tough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «A robust child» is a child who is strong and healthy and rarely ill. Robust is often used for things too: «a robust bike» is strongly made and not easy to break.
explain: Robust can also describe a plan or method that keeps working well in many conditions. A robust plan does not fall apart at the first problem, so look for clues in the words around it, such as what happens when things go wrong.
explain: Grown-up writers use robust for arguments too. «A robust discussion» means a heated argument, not a gentle chat. It is official language, so you may meet it in news reports. Swap in a word like strong or fierce and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Robust means strong, sturdy and not easy to break.
fact: «A robust child» is strong and healthy.
fact: «A robust bike» is strongly made, and «a robust plan» keeps working in many conditions.
fact: «A robust discussion» means a heated argument; it is official language.
fact: Food or drink can be robust too: a robust flavour is strong and full.
exercise: «The robust bike came through the rough park without a scratch.» What does robust mean here? | Very small and light | Painted bright red | Slow and noisy | *Strongly made and hard to break
exercise: The science team says their method is robust because it still works when the data are messy. What does robust mean? | Very old and rusty | Too sweet to eat | *Able to keep working well even when things are messy | Quiet and shy
exercise: «Tom is a ___ boy who is rarely ill.» Which word fits best? | Fragile | Glum | *Robust | Barely
test:  «A robust discussion» in the news means what? | A quiet chat over tea | A map of a city | A short holiday | *A heated argument
test: Which is the best clue that a plan is robust? | *It still works when things go wrong | It is written in pencil | It is very long | It falls apart at the first problem
exam: Mia says robust means rude. Why might she be wrong? | Robust means grey and wet | Robust means short and rude, like curt | Robust means very old | *Robust means strong or sturdy, not rude
